==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[throw]] [[off]]}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[confuse]]; especially, to [[lose]] a [[pursue]]r.
#: ''I never saw her without glasses before, so it '''threw me off''' when she got contact lenses.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To introduce [[error]]s or [[inaccuracies]]; to [[skew]].
#: ''The dirt in the apparatus '''threw off''' the results.''

